# Qualcomm QNN / QAIRT C API headers (4.0 NPU tier). FETCHED, NEVER COMMITTED.
# Every file under this tree carries "Confidential and Proprietary - Qualcomm Technologies, Inc."
# Compiling against them is what they are shipped for; redistributing them is not permitted, and
# this repo has a public remote. tools/fetch_qnn_headers.py re-fetches the pinned version on demand
# (and falls back to the local spike copy offline), so nothing is lost by keeping them out.
app/src/main/cpp/include/QNN/

# Proprietary blob SHAPES (4.1 L6) — defence in depth around the QNN extraction. The entry above
# is exact-path only, so a header copied one directory too high, or a libQnnHtp.so extracted from
# the AAR to sideload, would be stageable by `git add -A` — and the extractQnnSkel task extracts
# exactly such a blob (libQnnHtpV75Skel.so). That extraction lands in the build directory, outside
# the repo, so these are the second line, not the only one. Nothing tracked matches any of the
# four (verified with `git ls-files` when they were added), so this untracks nothing.
*.so
*.dlc
*.context
app/src/main/cpp/include/Qnn*.h

# (4.2 F8) The acceptance session's logcat capture. The run-book writes it to
# C:\Users\bastr\.androidbuild\capture.txt — outside the repo, on purpose — so this line should
# never fire. It is here as belt-and-braces for the one realistic way it would: an owner mid-
# session, phone in one hand, typing a shorter relative redirect than the sheet's. This whole
# branch's discipline gates on `git status --porcelain` being empty, and a stray capture file
# would make the tree dirty at exactly the moment nobody wants to debug why.
capture.txt
